WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:09.119
In a room, the direct sound reaches the listener first, along the shortest path from the source.

2
00:00:10.604 --> 00:00:17.263
Then come the reflections off the walls. Each one travels a longer path: it arrives later and weaker.

3
00:00:18.606 --> 00:00:28.135
The reflections multiply until they form a reverberation tail. The walls absorb part of the energy at each bounce: with more absorption, the tail is shorter.

4
00:00:33.181 --> 00:00:40.756
A resonance is a frequency the system reinforces, like a guitar body or a room mode. In the spectrum it shows up as a peak.
